{"id": "EUVD-2026-93200", "enisaUuid": "549cdb24-f427-3e0e-80f9-4f520f250752", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: mvpp2: prevent buffer overflow in page_pool allocation\n\nThe per\u2011processor buffering scheme is supported only if the\nnumber of pools (nrxqs\u202f*\u202f2) does not exceed MVPP2_BM_MAX_POOLS (8).\nThis is already checked in mvpp2_probe() during the initial\nactivation of percpu_pools.\n\nHowever, mvpp2_change_mtu() may later call\nmvpp2_bm_switch_buffers(priv, true) without this check, which can\nlead to an out-of-bounds access in the priv->page_pool array in\nmvpp2_bm_init(). The array is sized to hold MVPP2_PORT_MAX_RXQ\nentries, and mvpp2_get_nrxqs() may return exactly that value. The\nper-CPU scheme then doubles it to nrxqs * 2, exceeding the array\nbounds.\n\nCheck that the hardware version is MVPP22 or newer and that the\nnumber of pools (nrxqs * 2) does not exceed MVPP2_BM_MAX_POOLS\nbefore switching to per-CPU mode.\n\nFound by Linux Verification Center (linuxtesting.org) with SVACE.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:44", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5cefdb7acfc646fbded59ae77dfe0aac4c9e4a3c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ac1d5adc4f4dbafbfd270b55cc6d8bf9849d545", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dfd46b5584a5881b131008767950e1ab82713c8c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6569fd85b0ef9a8a6f20b7eb868420b8c7c0c2a0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7f30dcfa6c64033bf9137362517bd248e5be384", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f0e7d62c1eb984dd204095118973c59604144cd8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1734c3fc0066e228ce1c11e434b7c2527f0a949a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/14cb1e7702e5cb3c58888f6aed498381a73927d2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98272", "GHSA-986m-q5f3-3m78"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09e82432-65f0-328a-b76d-a8fe2be907d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1dc0389f-562d-3c7e-bef3-118752656538", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7d04b0b13b1175ce0c4bdc77f1278c1f120f874f <e7f30dcfa6c64033bf9137362517bd248e5be384"}, {"id": "25d09fda-9d14-34ff-89cc-fbd6c3fde311", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7d04b0b13b1175ce0c4bdc77f1278c1f120f874f <14cb1e7702e5cb3c58888f6aed498381a73927d2"}, {"id": "290998e0-a9c1-361a-b5e2-4fabb29da047", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "409a88d1-c9df-3d6a-9b3b-4249b7d51da9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "4e79db6d-642e-39e6-85f7-af2751c1cfc0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7d04b0b13b1175ce0c4bdc77f1278c1f120f874f <dfd46b5584a5881b131008767950e1ab82713c8c"}, {"id": "667afc01-6c83-37d6-abb6-317c974e71a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7d04b0b13b1175ce0c4bdc77f1278c1f120f874f <6569fd85b0ef9a8a6f20b7eb868420b8c7c0c2a0"}, {"id": "74e70360-229e-3021-9509-c7c3497f805a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "754c689c-8635-3551-a4a2-5ade4d72423d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "81fb9dcc-8140-3fe9-b29c-668bf1f6b991", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "a3e45a8a-f6ba-30af-a4cf-2e10a776b8ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7d04b0b13b1175ce0c4bdc77f1278c1f120f874f <f0e7d62c1eb984dd204095118973c59604144cd8"}, {"id": "aac231f8-469c-31f0-a4bb-dddf87de90d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.4"}, {"id": "b0b1abd1-f7df-30a0-99cc-6e55ea878e